[a] per process look at /proc/$1/status VMRss is the actual size in the RAM VMSize is the total size will include pages not committed to 
the RAM.

[b] There is /proc/$1/smaps_rollup

[c] For detailed memory map look at smaps (RSS/swap and so forth)

[d] To get an idea of what process is using up RAM do top and look at VMRss or use memmon /usr/bin/memmonitory.py requires root 
priv though.

[e] to get a more detailed system level overview stare at /proc/meminfo

